    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1940893317597716658",
      "url": "https://x.com/NDRRMC_OpCen/status/1940893317597716658",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/NDRRMC_OpCen/status/1940893317597716658",
      "text": "WEATHER UPDATE | 24-HOUR PUBLIC WEATHER FORECAST\nIssued at 4:00 AM, 04 July 2025\n\nSYNOPSIS: At 3:00 AM today, the center of Tropical Depression \"BISING\" was estimated based on all available data at 200 km West Northwest of Calayan, Cagayan (19.7°N, 119.6°E) with maximum sustained winds of 45 km/h near the center and gustiness of up to 55 km/h. It is moving Southwestward at 20 km/h. Southwest Monsoon affecting Central and Southern Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao.\n\nForecast Weather Conditions\n\nArea: Ilocos Norte and Babuyan Islands\nWeather Condition: Rains with Gusty winds\nCaused By: TD BISING\nImpacts: Possible flooding or landslides due to moderate to heavy rains. Minimal to minor threat to lives and properties due to strong winds.\n\nArea: Apayao, Kalinga, Abra, Batanes, and mainland Cagayan\nWeather Condition: Cloudy skies with scattered rains and thunderstorms\nCaused By: TD BISING\nImpacts: Possible flash floods or landslides due to moderate to heavy rains\n\nArea: Metro Manila, Pampanga, Tarlac, Bulacan, Zambales, Bataan, Cavite, Batangas, Occidental Mindoro, and the rest of Ilocos Region and Cordillera Administrative Region\nWeather Condition: Occasional rains\nCaused By: Southwest Monsoon\nImpacts: Possible flash floods or landslides due to moderate to heavy rains\n\nArea: Visayas, Dinagat Islands, Surigao del Norte, and the rest of Luzon\nWeather Condition: Cloudy skies with scattered rains and thunderstorms\nCaused By: Southwest Monsoon\nImpacts: Possible flash floods or landslides due to moderate to at times heavy rains\n\nArea: The rest of the country\nWeather Condition: Partly cloudy to cloudy skies with isolated rainshowers or thunderstorms\nCaused By: Southwest Monsoon\nImpacts: Possible flash floods or landslides during severe thunderstorms\n\nForecast Wind and Coastal Water Conditions\n\nArea: Northern Luzon\nWind Speed: Moderate to Strong\nWind Direction: Southwest to South\nCoastal Waters: Moderate to Rough / (1.2 to 2.5 meters)\n\nArea: The rest of the country\nWind Speed: Light to Moderate\nWind Direction: Southwest\nCoastal Waters: Slight to Moderate / (0.6 to 2.1 meters)\n\nExtremes of Temperature and Relative Humidity for The 24-hour Period Ending 8:00 PM YESTERDAY\n\nMinimum Temperature: 24.2 °C ... 7:20 AM\nMaximum Temperature: 27.6 °C... 2:00 PM\n\nMinumum Relative Humidity: 85 % ... 2:00 PM\nMaximum Relative Humidity: 95 % ... 2:00 AM\n\nTIDES AND ASTRONOMICAL INFORMATION Over Metro Manila\n\nLow Tide TODAY: 12:23PM ... 0.54\nLow Tide TODAY: 10:15PM ... 0.42\nHigh Tide TODAY: 05:30AM ... 0.8\nHigh Tide TODAY: 4:07PM ... 0.61\n\nsunrise today: 5:32AM\nsunset today: 6:30PM\nmoonrise today: 1:00PM\nmoonset today: 12:12AM\nillumination today: 66%\n\nFor other information about weather, please log on to https://t.co/pOzFfDt64P or https://t.co/LGM78fwelr or call at (02)927-1335/(02)926-4258\n\nSource: DOST-PAGASA\n\n#NDRRMC\n#BawatSegundoMahalaga\n#BisingPH",
